__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# validation-run/ and validation-inputs/ are deliberately NOT ignored.
# They are the evidence base: src/data/protocol.js cites run records by path
# ("run records in validation-run/full-screen/"), and a claim whose evidence is
# untracked is a claim nobody can check. ~9 MB total, small enough for plain git.

# The ZINC decoy source library is the one exception to the rule above. It is
# ~126 MB, it is not evidence, and it is not ours: it is a slice of ZINC20
# fetched by fetch_decoy_library.py, which records exactly which tranches and
# shards were pulled in library_manifest.json. The manifest is the reproducible
# artefact; the bytes are not worth a repository.
validation-inputs/enrichment/zinc_library.smi
